} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355210} {:answer/id #uuid "4560de0c-70f4-51f5-a9a3-63faf56a8b0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355280} {:answer/id #uuid "b4d7c148-b989-57f1-b1ac-86ad209009b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356254} {:answer/id #uuid "e7836302-9e53-590b-81c4-7e3b4b7e7bce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356688}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4560de0c-70f4-51f5-a9a3-63faf56a8b0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355280} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d1ba9a3-81a9-5dc9-9598-2c7b40e1e779" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356967}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1738a08a-0e6c-5ca9-b9ee-772359397eb8" :question/math-academy-id "q-92995" :question/problem "Find the root of $f(x)={e}^{x}-{e}^{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n{e}^{x}-{e}^{4}=0\n$$\n\nFirst, we isolate the term with the variable exponent by adding ${e}^{4}$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}-{e}^{4} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{x}-\\cancel{{e}^{4}}+\\cancel{{e}^{4}} & =0+{e}^{4} \\\\ {e}^{x} & ={e}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since both sides of the equation share the same base $e$, we equate the exponents. This gives\n\n$$\nx=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357540 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115203 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee02c223-dd7f-5c5d-b09f-e7bc6bd16b0c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Root of a Transformed Exponential Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "024cb00d-23a5-5998-a7e2-0ef6f494abe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354676} {:answer/id #uuid "35ac62bd-1fa9-5ff6-bc3a-d5415133874f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355149} {:answer/id #uuid "4ff56156-dec0-5625-887c-a6a00810f413" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355376} {:answer/id #uuid "5045dc71-23e2-5c2f-aeb5-cf26fed94158" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355380} {:answer/id #uuid "d787633f-7310-59a3-a889-9935ea02f4fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356550}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d787633f-7310-59a3-a889-9935ea02f4fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356550} :answer-field/id #uuid "742646f8-b0b0-5de6-aa67-6e561c90e6e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357124}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dc356c61-c382-5786-b505-51f9c59fb0a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-92998" :question/problem "Find the root of $f(x)=4{e}^{2x-1}-8.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n4{e}^{2x-1}-8=0\n$$\n\nFirst, we isolate the term with the variable exponent by adding $8$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{e}^{2x-1}-8 & =0 \\\\ 4{e}^{2x-1}-\\cancel{8}+\\cancel{8} & =0+8 \\\\ 4{e}^{2x-1} & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing both sides by $4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{e}^{2x-1} & =8 \\\\ {e}^{2x-1} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen we take $ln$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2x-1} & =2 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2x-1}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ 2x-1 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-1 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ 2x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+1 \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357743 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083226 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc94085c-4088-5eaf-887a-eea7f040573c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Z-Score of a Given Observation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "268ee764-f4ba-5bb4-b9a6-25d0217bbe25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.01" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354988} {:answer/id #uuid "46057ddc-18e7-5373-90a9-8e327b81e327" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355286} {:answer/id #uuid "9818d993-5599-51c2-be03-5470aa4ffc0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.91" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356007} {:answer/id #uuid "99b6d8a4-b90d-5fc6-aad9-00a4aaa9f246" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.46" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356029} {:answer/id #uuid "e518197b-b17c-5f90-b633-521d029c1507" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46057ddc-18e7-5373-90a9-8e327b81e327" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355286} :answer-field/id #uuid "23bf6b9f-ca8a-544b-9d4e-a0a158f07d3d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356977}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e38779e8-5306-5b5e-a170-45db52e7f21d" :question/math-academy-id "q-94457" :question/problem "A data set has mean $\\overset{―}{x}=6$ and variance ${\\sigma }^{2}=10.8.$ Find the $z$-score of an observation $x=10.5,$ giving your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The $z$-score of an observation $x$ is defined by\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{x-\\overset{―}{x}}{\\sigma }.\n$$\n\nThe $z$-score represents how many standard deviations an observation is above or below the mean of the data set.\n\nHere, we're told that the mean is $\\overset{―}{x}=6,$ and we can calculate the standard deviation as\n\n$$\n\\sigma =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}}=\\sqrt{10.8}.\n$$\n\nSo, the $z$-score of the observation $x=10.5$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{x-\\overset{―}{x}}{\\sigma } \\\\  & ≈\\frac{10.5-6}{\\sqrt{10.8}} \\\\  & ≈1.37\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto $2$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357744 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083226 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc94085c-4088-5eaf-887a-eea7f040573c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Z-Score of a Given Observation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "202f2ede-33d8-5d23-a897-b75e4b1cc459" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7.38" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354933} {:answer/id #uuid "4ccb96c7-be37-57f3-af85-a3d9641697ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5.23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355348} {:answer/id #uuid "4e12e047-e3d4-5a77-974e-be93c594e33c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.43" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355357} {:answer/id #uuid "b276c159-4f0a-5ba8-bcf1-27b7f26ed839" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356235} {:answer/id #uuid "baadf541-5610-5499-940a-702e8f2b4f15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "202f2ede-33d8-5d23-a897-b75e4b1cc459" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7.38" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354933} :answer-field/id #uuid "beb393c6-1b84-5f14-9647-ac0b4335c2a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357260}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "694368b5-e718-5efc-b12c-37e7e99e29bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-94460" :question/problem "A data set has mean $\\overset{―}{x}=28$ and variance ${\\sigma }^{2}=3.60.$ Find the $z$-score of an observation $x=14,$ giving your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The $z$-score of an observation $x$ is defined by\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{x-\\overset{―}{x}}{\\sigma }.\n$$\n\nThe $z$-score represents how many standard deviations an observation is above or below the mean of the data set.\n\nHere, we're told that the mean is $\\overset{―}{x}=28,$ and we can calculate the standard deviation as\n\n$$\n\\sigma =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}}=\\sqrt{3.60}.\n$$\n\nSo, the $z$-score of the observation $x=14$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{x-\\overset{―}{x}}{\\sigma } \\\\  & ≈\\frac{14-28}{\\sqrt{3.60}} \\\\  & ≈-7.38\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto $2$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357745 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083227 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2169053d-78fc-5714-82f4-d89fc36ff695" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Observation, Standard Deviation, or Mean Given a Z-Score"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2bcca9d-4ee4-558c-ac6d-3dba6fed8a3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356239} {:answer/id #uuid "d8efc532-df6e-5410-bc77-a7e5779ef469" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356568} {:answer/id #uuid "db1c6fb0-f620-582c-930f-ddf023b658c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.78" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356592} {:answer/id #uuid "e8af3748-e949-5d0a-b0f5-6cde72841fd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.92" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356698} {:answer/id #uuid "f9242971-1fcf-5df3-b81b-b36d9bd54094" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356839}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8efc532-df6e-5410-bc77-a7e5779ef469" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356568} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f71beb9-8e13-54e1-a94f-41a8e740e60f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357046}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "530121a9-23c4-5834-af6f-63e88a6adfa0" :question/math-academy-id "q-94471" :question/problem "A data set has a mean $\\overset{¯}{x}=14.5$ and an unknown standard deviation. An observation of the data set has the value $x=20$ and $z$-score $z=2.2.$ Find the standard deviation of the data set." :question/worked-solution "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{―}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=20,$ $\\overset{¯}{x}=14.5,$ and $z=2.2$ into the formula and solving for $\\sigma ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 20 & =14.5+2.2\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 5.5 & =2.2\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ \\sigma  & =2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357752 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083322 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7e9daa2-4aaa-5c33-b611-231f3d0e4782" :knowledge-point/title "Z-Score: Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1faf19fd-0dd5-586e-926d-6340b195ba2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.8\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354930} {:answer/id #uuid "49216ee7-3d5e-58e3-a5fb-5cdd2a0d69f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.0\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355310} {:answer/id #uuid "8b6197b1-b81b-52af-b216-72cc6a553860" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.2\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355897} {:answer/id #uuid "d597713f-c6b1-5820-b22a-210e4633ed35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356535} {:answer/id #uuid "e81a51df-4cdd-5475-bfa1-e5313586a540" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.0\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1faf19fd-0dd5-586e-926d-6340b195ba2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.8\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354930} :answer-field/id #uuid "366f682e-3735-536c-b4a3-11af61adcace" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357005}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1fa2412f-8859-5e81-9fb7-100702a88998" :question/math-academy-id "q-94519" :question/problem "The mean weight of a group of ballet dancers is $45\\text{ kg}.$ One of the dancers in the ballet group weighs $38\\text{ kg}$, and her $z$-score is $-2.5.$ Find the standard deviation of the weight of the dancers in the ballet group." :question/worked-solution "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{―}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=38,$ $\\overset{―}{x}=45,$ and $z=-2.5$ into the formula and solving for $\\sigma ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 38 & =45+(-2.5)\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ -7 & =-2.5\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{-7}{-2.5} \\\\ \\sigma  & =2.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the standard deviation of the ballet dancer's weights is $2.8\\,\\text{kg}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362243 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083322 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7e9daa2-4aaa-5c33-b611-231f3d0e4782" :knowledge-point/title "Z-Score: Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19447168-1474-5be9-aac6-ad97fed12bd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.61" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360937} {:answer/id #uuid "1fe70794-f488-59e6-afbe-8f9bdce41f92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.57" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360972} {:answer/id #uuid "26497c17-1e52-5f13-9672-7d7541e882bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361001} {:answer/id #uuid "2e772d5a-11ce-5758-badf-fef6f326e8c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361044} {:answer/id #uuid "ed84d4c8-52d6-5fed-ade3-9113944fe3ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.57" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361893}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fe70794-f488-59e6-afbe-8f9bdce41f92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.57" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360972} :answer-field/id #uuid "a007c32a-4b84-5c4e-9daf-279e1005a6e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362130}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a38c82cd-ff4b-53d8-85bc-f102ff90d451" :question/math-academy-id "q-9785" :question/problem "The mean weight of a group of newborn children is $3.2kg$ with a standard deviation of $350g.$\nWhat is the $z$-score that corresponds to a weight of $3kg?$ Give your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $350g=0.350kg$\n\nThe $z$-score of an observation $x$ is defined by\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{x-\\overset{―}{x}}{\\sigma }.\n$$\n\nThe $z$-score represents how many standard deviations an observation is above or below the mean of the data set.\n\nSo, the $z$-score of the observation $x=3$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{x-\\overset{¯}{x}}{\\sigma } \\\\  & =\\frac{3-3.2}{0.350} \\\\  & =-0.57\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nto $2$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395363 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "52e11164-1929-594d-9f9e-460f6469421d" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing a Stretched Negative 